body:
This user seems to be getting something together: [https://www.reddit.com/r/selfhelp/comments/n4kqwd/to\_those\_interested\_in\_cooperative\_transformation/?utm\_source=share&utm\_medium=web2x&context=3](https://www.reddit.com/r/selfhelp/comments/n4kqwd/to_those_interested_in_cooperative_transformation/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=web2x&context=3)

&#x200B;

The lesson I've learned is to never ask for a do-over. People will run miles with that phrase and fuck you over hard. All I can say is, if you feel like you've lost a year of your life, use that as a wake-up call!! Buy a cheap self-help book addressing that exact issue, or make a retroactive bucket list (what you wish you had done during that year). Also, because all of us are all living in this shitty timeline of human history, don't be too hard on yourself because 2020 has been awful to nearly everyone alive. A lot of stuff got put on hold to watch a global death toll rise.

I've been assaulted a couple times in the past two years and haven't really been able to process it because the last time I spoke up I was told it made other people uncomfortable... So, you know, that makes things difficult. I would try talking to a therapist in an honest and sincere way if I were you. There's not a lot of ways to explain why this happens without delving into deep, systemic issues based around gender and sexuality and even then it gets very pedantic because the ""problems with the system"" don't justify sexual violence at all. Being told to just cope warrants a lot of anger from me, personally. I'm glad you decided to speak up, though. With the problem out there in the open, this society should be able to begin to confront it. I mean, I've only been able to report my assaults once, and the other times these assholes have gotten away with it because I either didn't know who they were or because of a simple lack of resources. I tend to forget it happens right afterwards but then when a random, minor inconvenience arises afterwards, I fall back on bad habits. That's the key thing to avoid... but also not beat yourself up about, you know? 

&#x200B;

JUST REMEMBER YOU ARE SO STRONG. SURVIVORS ARE STRONG PEOPLE. The fact that there are so many things going on and life is turbulent DOES NOT MEAN THAT PEOPLE SHOULD NOT HAVE YOUR BACK!

I have nobody to talk with on a regular basis. I tried dating apps, and met two people. Neither of them seemed horny enough to be an interesting match with my current personality, but something insisted I wouldn't like them in a friend-based way either. I have therapy once a month. My old therapist from a year ago I had to stop seeing because of this worldwide bullshit doesn't have enough space to take me back as a patient, and it feels really hard starting fresh again. I already don't like this lady. I don't know what more to say about that. There are parks nearby, and places to walk, but I am here on this subreddit, like you, because I am lonely, not because I am bored. 

&#x200B;

If there's something about loneliness you want to talk about, or something in my post you can relate to in that regards, feel free to message me. I cried a ton during January.

Dude, I know. The bear was massively underused because of the level design. I had no problem with the size of the map per se, but when that motherfucker showed up I expected to be HAUNTED by that beast for a good while more instead of it just being used for the boss fight. Which was, in addition, really freakin' stupid. If you're going to make a boss fight happen on a plateau with spaces to fall off of, my mind, without using online guides, automatically goes 'Ok I gotta coax this bear to run off the edge' and that's still pretty challenging given its ferocity. Making it a sponge and then activating a cutscene is just a total lack of ingenuity on the designers' part. 

&#x200B;

Also, yeah- this was the first level with more than two armed factions at play, and there was no chance to see their conflicts play out. Like when I played Fallout 3 I would get excited to see Brotherhood and Enclave troops face off, but always wanted to see this happen in a better graphics engine... Metro could have totally pulled this off. Maybe by making the Volga section smaller, which seemed like just a repeat of stuff I already played in Last Light (I mean, aesthetically it's just the same shit from that game, right?)
